- op: discuss  # 98d0
  at: '2026-04-25T22:01:30Z'  # 98d0
  by: agent  # 98d0
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 98d0
  clock: 3  # 98d0
  nonce: 98d0  # 98d0
  message: "Root cause identified. The WI-darad fix (commit 5fff57205) correctly populates leaf_callers / entry_points_per_leaf in compute_boundary_map (io_boundary.py:939-967). However, cmd_io_boundaries (cli.py:3233-3239) reconstructs BoundaryMapEntry without those two fields when the filter path triggers — and the filter path triggers whenever `primitive_filter or exclude_tests` is true. Since exclude_tests=True is the default (WI-sifif), the strip happens for every normal CLI invocation, including bakeoff. Confirmed against cohort-001/iter-010 alertmanager: every boundary has chain_count>0 but leaf_callers=[] and entry_points_per_leaf={}. This is structural, not a claim error or unfair cohort. Plan: extract a _compute_leaf_rollups helper from compute_boundary_map; have the CLI filter path call _build_reverse_graph + _compute_leaf_rollups to recompute the rollups for the filtered chain subset. TDD red test will assert leaf_callers is non-empty in JSON output with default args. Will reopen WI-darad's awaits_bakeoff_validation tag scope after fix lands."  # 98d0
